Subject: lottie: trim paths "individually" across groups as one sequence

A trim path set to "Trim Multiple Shapes: Individually" trims every path below it as one
sequence, also the paths of the groups under it (After Effects, lottie-web). ThorVG draws each
group that paints (a stroke of its own) as a shape of its own and gave every shape the whole
trim range, so each group was trimmed on its own: other parts of the paths showed, e.g. dots
of round caps where nothing should be drawn (Lordicon: 188 public icons trim this way).

The builder now collects the shapes made under such a trim and, once the group is built, shares
the range out over them in stacking order, by the length of their paths; a shape outside the
range draws nothing. The paths of the groups under the trim are reversed as patch 08 does for
the trim's own group, so that they too reach the trimming in stacking order.

Origin: Lordicon.
Base: thorvg/thorvg main 72a66415 (1.2.0). License: MIT, like ThorVG.
